# Integrity lock for the evaluator-owned files of the LOCAL LIVE-MODEL
# SUPERVISOR ACCEPTANCE GATE (spec: /tmp/lv-supervisor-local-acceptance-spec.md,
# sha256 3ed295730058e053a001d831dc5ed937e860d0fca6dae2ae7b3311ac80de337a;
# architecture: /tmp/lv-autonomous-live-content-architecture.md, sha256
# 4704227a99b84089a7fead2ed39b2b605b884edf903d9d65261c930f78071758).
#
# FIFTH EVAL-OWNER FREEZE: re-frozen after a full live execution proved one
# remaining CHECKER deadlock — the same same-process loopback defect, reached
# INDIRECTLY through an imported production wrapper. No production change could
# fix it, and none is required.
#
# THE DEFECT. `local-acceptance-live-ship.eval.mjs` C-N13-outcome called
# `prod.recordSupervisorOutcome(payload)` and supplied no coordinatorFn.
# Production `recordSupervisorOutcome({...}, coordinatorFn = coordinator)` then
# defaulted to `coordinator()`, whose body launches
# `scripts/automation/coordinator.mjs` through the synchronous
# `command`/`execFileSync` path. Because the fake GitHub double is hosted in the
# EVALUATOR's own Node event loop, that child completed its loopback TCP connect
# and then waited forever for a response the blocked host could never write:
# observed >3 minutes at 0% CPU on `record-candidate-outcome --outcome
# MONITOR_TIMEOUT`. A frozen path therefore does not have to WRITE a synchronous
# spawn to deadlock the checker — calling a production wrapper that DEFAULTS to
# one is the identical defect one level down.
#
# THE EVALUATOR-ONLY FIX.
#
# (1) C-N13-outcome now injects the eval-owned bounded async
#     `asyncCoordinatorSeam().fn` through the coordinatorFn seam production
#     ALREADY exposes (helpers/acceptance-exec.mjs). The seam mirrors the
#     production wrapper exactly — private GITHUB_OUTPUT file, appended `--repo`,
#     key=value parse, throw on a nonzero exit — but launches the child async,
#     detached into its own process group, under a short per-call bound with a
#     process-group SIGKILL sweep. No production wrapper becomes async and no
#     approved behavior changes. The check still proves everything it did
#     before and MORE: production's own argument mapping (subcommand, --kind,
#     --outcome, --key, --topic-key, --reason after boundedOutcomeReason, and
#     the appended --repo), the terminal outcome it forwards, exit 0,
#     `recorded=true`, the durable `automation-state: blog candidate ladder`
#     issue carrying MONITOR_TIMEOUT, and that no child process survived
#     (helpers/acceptance-scenario.mjs `recordOutcomeThroughSeam`).
#
# (2) FULL INDIRECT AUDIT of every frozen eval call into an imported production
#     function while the in-process double is listening. Only two production
#     surfaces reachable from a frozen path can spawn synchronously:
#     `recordSupervisorOutcome` (fixed above, via its coordinatorFn seam) and
#     `monitorOwnedPr`, which redispatches through the synchronous
#     `coordinator()` only when BOTH automation/ci and automation/opus-gate are
#     missing past LOST_STATUS_MS. C-N13-setup now ASSERTS both contexts are
#     posted at the pinned head, so that branch is provably unreachable in the
#     one place the monitor is driven in-process. Everything else the evaluator
#     calls in-process (validatePaths, validatePullRequest, validateIngest*,
#     terminalFromObservation, statusForExactSha, latestAuditForSha,
#     finalizeOwnedPr, evaluateSentinel, readLedger, candidate-state renderers,
#     resolveLintMode, boundedOutcomeReason, terminalRequiresCandidateOutcome)
#     reaches no child process at all. The remaining execFileSync calls in the
#     frozen set are local git/CLI work that never contacts the double
#     (local-git-fixture, fake-supervisor-protection, the orchestrator's
#     git/pi/npm `run`, and the double's own scrubbed-env blog-lint), and
#     loadPiSdk's `npm root --global` runs in the environment phase before any
#     double exists.
#
# (3) local-acceptance-deadlock.eval.mjs regression EXTENDED to both shapes and
#     re-proven discriminating. DL4 now scans every manifest-listed file for a
#     DIRECT synchronous child carrying the double AND for an INDIRECT call into
#     a registered production sync-spawn wrapper with no injected async seam
#     (PRODUCTION_SYNC_SPAWN_WRAPPERS / ASYNC_SEAM_MARKERS in
#     helpers/acceptance-exec.mjs). Comments are stripped and calls SPELLED
#     inside string literals are ignored, so prose and registry entries are never
#     mistaken for calls. New DL4b proves the scan still discriminates in four
#     directions on synthetic sources (seamless wrapper call flagged; the same
#     call with the seam not flagged; a wrapper named only in prose not flagged;
#     a direct sync child carrying the double flagged). New DL6 is a bounded
#     DYNAMIC reproduction of the exact C-N13-outcome shape against the REAL
#     production wrapper with a stub coordinator planted at the exact path
#     production resolves: DL6-negative proves the SYNCHRONOUS default is served
#     nothing by the server it blocks, and DL6 proves the seam-injected call
#     completes, is served, maps every argument, leaves a durable
#     MONITOR_TIMEOUT record, and leaves no orphan process.
#
# The file set is UNCHANGED at 15 eval-owned files. Every file below is
# eval-owned and FROZEN.
#
# These files are FROZEN. The implementation builder must not edit, weaken,
# delete, re-scope, or restage any of them. Maker != checker: any change to an
# eval-owned path is a spec/eval-owner change and an automatic FAIL of the
# acceptance review until the eval owner re-freezes.
